1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:02,298
Farmers can walk a field.

2
00:00:02,338 --> 00:00:04,688
But they cannot see infrared.

3
00:00:07,092 --> 00:00:09,262
Multispectral sensors can.

4
00:00:09,302 --> 00:00:12,866
In a peer-reviewed soybean drought study,
drone-based red-edge imagery revealed differences

5
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:15,116
between plots at day forty-six.

6
00:00:15,156 --> 00:00:18,637
Wilting became visible at day sixty-four—
eighteen days later.

7
00:00:18,677 --> 00:00:22,632
Sentinel-2 carries multispectral bands
across fields and seasons.

8
00:00:23,096 --> 00:00:25,321
These analyses exist.

9
00:00:25,361 --> 00:00:28,782
But finding clear images, aligning dates,
processing spectral bands,

10
00:00:28,822 --> 00:00:32,358
and interpreting results takes
specialist software and hours.

11
00:00:32,398 --> 00:00:37,888
Gemini 3.5 can coordinate the workflow and explain it
in language a farmer can use.

12
00:00:39,096 --> 00:00:40,974
Satellites measure.

13
00:00:41,014 --> 00:00:42,942
Gemini reasons.

14
00:00:42,982 --> 00:00:45,008
The farmer decides.

15
00:00:47,095 --> 00:00:51,078
Field mapping means collecting GPS points
and cleaning polygons.

16
00:00:51,118 --> 00:00:54,326
With 1415 Agri, one point becomes
a proposed boundary

17
00:00:54,366 --> 00:00:56,726
for the farmer to review and confirm.

18
00:00:56,766 --> 00:00:58,360
Two clicks.

19
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:01,648
Meet 1415 Agri.

20
00:01:05,092 --> 00:01:08,262
Gemini 3.5 Flash runs on Vertex AI.

21
00:01:08,302 --> 00:01:10,679
Google ADK routes requests.

22
00:01:10,719 --> 00:01:13,814
MCP exposes typed evidence and action tools.

23
00:01:13,854 --> 00:01:17,512
Deterministic services handle geometry
and pixel math.

24
00:01:18,096 --> 00:01:23,554
Now, a real family field in Taquarituba, Brazil:
soybeans, the 2025–26 season,

25
00:01:23,594 --> 00:01:26,710
about thirty-six hectares,
and one reference point.

26
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:28,828
Guided Demo is off.

27
00:01:28,868 --> 00:01:32,312
The system proposes the cultivated boundary;
the farmer reviews it,

28
00:01:32,352 --> 00:01:35,072
adjusts it if needed, and confirms.

29
00:01:40,096 --> 00:01:44,057
The request goes through Cloud Tasks
to a private Cloud Run worker.

30
00:01:44,097 --> 00:01:48,154
It searches real Sentinel-2 Level-2A imagery,
masks clouds, aligns dates,

31
00:01:48,194 --> 00:01:51,719
and calculates NDVI, NDRE, and NDMI.

32
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:54,983
This run finds five usable observations
from October through March

33
00:01:55,023 --> 00:01:57,495
and finishes in ninety-three seconds.

34
00:01:57,535 --> 00:02:01,968
The same analysis ID connects
every stage, artifact, and log.

35
00:02:05,096 --> 00:02:09,115
One season becomes four areas
with different spectral histories.

36
00:02:09,155 --> 00:02:13,363
Every highlight connects back to dates, index values,
source bands, cloud coverage,

37
00:02:13,403 --> 00:02:15,446
and Sentinel-2 provenance.

38
00:02:15,486 --> 00:02:18,108
Area One shows the clearest change.

39
00:02:18,148 --> 00:02:21,088
That is where the next field visit begins.

40
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:29,135
So the farmer asks a normal question:
“Why should I check Area One first,

41
00:02:29,175 --> 00:02:31,710
and what should I look for when I get there?”

42
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:36,360
Gemini calls the evidence tools and compares
this field's stored history.

43
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:40,998
It cites February twenty-second and March fourteenth,
explains the changes in NDVI,

44
00:02:41,038 --> 00:02:45,098
NDRE, and NDMI,
and gives three practical checks.

45
00:02:45,138 --> 00:02:49,698
The trace shows Gemini 3.5 Flash, Google ADK,
the temporal specialist,

46
00:02:49,738 --> 00:02:52,776
and every MCP tool behind the answer.

47
00:02:55,095 --> 00:02:56,991
Then Gemini acts.

48
00:02:57,031 --> 00:03:00,886
The farmer asks,
“Compare this field again using three areas.”

49
00:03:00,926 --> 00:03:05,083
The trace shows the temporal specialist calling
request_field_analysis,

50
00:03:05,123 --> 00:03:08,420
creating the new request,
and queuing the background job.

51
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:12,384
Idempotency makes retries safe
instead of duplicating work.

52
00:03:14,096 --> 00:03:16,310
The farmer rates the answer.

53
00:03:16,350 --> 00:03:20,584
That feedback stays linked to the exact
analysis and conversation.

54
00:03:21,096 --> 00:03:25,327
Here is the production system running on Google Cloud:
four permissioned Cloud Run services

55
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:30,242
for web, worker, MCP, and agent,
all from one immutable container.

56
00:03:30,282 --> 00:03:33,009
Vertex AI provides Gemini.

57
00:03:33,049 --> 00:03:35,717
Firestore stores state and evidence.

58
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:38,217
Cloud Storage stores artifacts.

59
00:03:38,257 --> 00:03:41,192
Cloud Tasks runs the satellite workflow.

60
00:03:41,232 --> 00:03:43,217
Cloud Logging records the worker request

61
00:03:43,257 --> 00:03:45,776
and the persisted analysis read.

62
00:03:48,095 --> 00:03:50,326
The signal was always there.

63
00:03:50,366 --> 00:03:52,681
Now small farmers can use it.

64
00:03:52,721 --> 00:03:55,592
1415 Agri.
